I am puzzled over the meaning of fit indices produced when running SEM models with grouping variables.

Specifically, although Lavaan reports separate Chi Square values for each group, it does not report separate RMSEA or other fit indices per group, but instead reports what appear to be overall fit indices.

I am not sure what these represent, and am hoping for some assistance.  To take one particular situation: if we set a constraint so that the groups have equal regression coefficients, would the fit indices represent the degree of fit for some overall model that includes the groups and/or constraint of equal regression coefficients?
What I am after is the separate fit indices for each group, assuming equal regression coefficients (or equal loadings, etc).

But perhaps reporting overall fit indices is a better solution for some reason or the other, I can't find anything in the documentation that clarifies this for me, and I can't reason my way through it either...

Thanks in advance,

