Here are the differences:

fit_2 freely estimate all thresholds while fits[[2]] fix some thresholds for identifications.
fit_2 fix all residual variances as 1 whereas fits[[2]] freely estimate residual variances.
fit_2 fix factor mean as 0 whereas fits[[2]] freely estimate factor means.

fits[[2]] follows the parameterization proposed by Millsap and Yun-Tein (2004). Because strict invariance has not been established yet so residual variances should not be fixed as 1. Thus, I would recommend you use the fits[[2]] as the weak invariance model.

