Subject: Standard errors: default delta method vs "first.order"
Message-ID: <ddqw0CCm1Vc.YQK097pompYJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/ddqw0CCm1Vc/m/YQK097pompYJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

     I am working on a mediation model, and I want to obtain the standard error for a derived parameter, ab, the product of two other parameters.  I think I read in some of Yves’ wonderful course materials that default standard errors are delta method, but there is an option for “first.order”, as well as “bootstrap”.  My question is about the distinction between delta method and “first.order.”  Is “first.order” a slightly simpler version of delta method, missing second order terms, or is the distinction between the two options about something else?

     Thanks.

--Ed Rigdon

