No, they are two separate applications....lavaanGUI uses the sem(), cfa() and growth() functions straight from the lavaan package....if you look at the form, you will see that all of the arguments map directly back into those three functions as defined in the Lavaan package. That is why the estimation is the same, if I understand your question correctly. The lavaanGUI app, which is really just a prototype, just sits on the same server with PLS-GUI. At any rate, I'd be happy to give you the source code for the version that I have, which I have always given away freely to anyone who asks for it.

