On 11/18/2014 05:42 PM, M. wrote:
> What would you recommend? Or is there actually a way to fix certain
> exogenous variables and leave others free within the same model?

You could 'upgrade' the ones that you would like to treat as 'random' to
latent variables. If they are called x1 and x2, you can write

fx1 =~ x1
fx2 =~ x2

and then use fx1 and fx2 as regressors in the model. All the others will
be 'fixed' by default.

But perhaps I should overload the fixed.x= argument by also accepting a
vector of variables names...

